rns. Also maybe bring up Candidate C's reliability and decision quality, but communication issues. She can argue that B remains best.\n\nShe should reference James' answer that D lacks specific reliability and stress evidence, and that D's arrogance and weak leadership are concerns. She can also note that we still lack reliability and stress data for A, making B strongest.\n\nThus Emily's public message: I agree with panel, still recommend B, because D lacks concrete reliability and stress evidence, and has crew cooperation concerns; A lacks reliability and stress data; C has communication issues; B covers core criteria.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
